     8	In conjunction with the Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) meeting held on
     9	September 15–16, 2026, meeting participants submitted their projections of the most
    10	likely outcomes for real gross domestic product (GDP) growth, the unemployment
    11	rate, and inflation for each year from 2026 to 2029 and over the longer run. Each
    12	participant’s projections were based on information available at the time of the meeting,
    13	together with her or his assessment of appropriate monetary policy—including a path
    14	for the federal funds rate and its longer-run value—and assumptions about other
    15	factors likely to affect economic outcomes. The longer-run projections represent each
    16	participant’s assessment of the value to which each variable would be expected to
    17	converge, over time, under appropriate monetary policy and in the absence of further
    18	shocks to the economy. “Appropriate monetary policy” is defined as the future path of
    19	policy that each participant deems most likely to foster outcomes for economic activity
    20	and inflation that best satisfy his or her individual interpretation of the statutory
    21	mandate to promote maximum employment and price stability.
