  1147	     Note: The blue and red lines are based on actual values and median projected values, respectively, of the
  1148	Committee’s target for the federal funds rate at the end of the year indicated. The actual values are the midpoint of
  1149	the target range; the median projected values are based on either the midpoint of the target range or the target level.
  1150	The confidence interval around the median projected values is based on root mean squared errors of various private
  1151	and government forecasts made over the previous 20 years. The confidence interval is not strictly consistent with the
  1152	projections for the federal funds rate, primarily because these projections are not forecasts of the likeliest outcomes for
  1153	the federal funds rate, but rather projections of participants’ individual assessments of appropriate monetary policy.
  1154	Still, historical forecast errors provide a broad sense of the uncertainty around the future path of the federal funds rate
  1155	generated by the uncertainty about the macroeconomic variables as well as additional adjustments to monetary policy
  1156	that may be appropriate to offset the effects of shocks to the economy.
  1157	     The confidence interval is assumed to be symmetric except when it is truncated at zero - the bottom of the lowest
  1158	target range for the federal funds rate that has been adopted in the past by the Committee. This truncation would
  1159	not be intended to indicate the likelihood of the use of negative interest rates to provide additional monetary policy
  1160	accommodation if doing so was judged appropriate. In such situations, the Committee could also employ other tools,
  1161	including forward guidance and large-scale asset purchases, to provide additional accommodation. Because current
  1162	conditions may differ from those that prevailed, on average, over the previous 20 years, the width and shape of the
  1163	confidence interval estimated on the basis of the historical forecast errors may not reflect FOMC participants’ current
  1164	assessments of the uncertainty and risks around their projections.
  1165	     * The confidence interval is derived from forecasts of the average level of short-term interest rates in the fourth
  1166	quarter of the year indicated; more information about these data is available in table 2. The shaded area encompasses
  1167	less than a 70 percent confidence interval if the confidence interval has been truncated at zero.
