data/sources/fed-rate/coverage/dow-jones-bessent-rate-hike-2026-08-31.txt-2-
data/sources/fed-rate/coverage/dow-jones-bessent-rate-hike-2026-08-31.txt-3-By Jessica Coacci
data/sources/fed-rate/coverage/dow-jones-bessent-rate-hike-2026-08-31.txt-4-Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said he is not going to speculate on what the Federal Reserve might do at its September interest rate meeting.
data/sources/fed-rate/coverage/dow-jones-bessent-rate-hike-2026-08-31.txt:5:But he did list a few reasons holding rates in place might make sense. "We've seen a supply shock, and traditionally you don't raise [rates]...unless you see second or third-order effects," Bessent said in an interview on CNBC.
data/sources/fed-rate/coverage/dow-jones-bessent-rate-hike-2026-08-31.txt-6-Bessent said core inflation has remained very restrained, and there will be a productivity boom on the other side of the AI-buildout.
data/sources/fed-rate/coverage/dow-jones-bessent-rate-hike-2026-08-31.txt-7-After Fed Chairman Kevin Warsh's debut speech at Jackson Hole Friday, odds for a September rate hike rose to nearly 60%, according to CME's FedWatch tool. They recently stood at about 66%.
data/sources/fed-rate/coverage/dow-jones-bessent-rate-hike-2026-08-31.txt-8-This item is part of a Wall Street Journal live coverage event. The full stream can be found by searching P/WSJL (WSJ Live Coverage).
